A||||14||86SE||The squeeking belt saga continues............||||8||
Z||000000||86SE||06-26-2000||02:05 AM||||How do you tighten these damn belts?  It (the squeeking) has gotten WAY worse.  Just testing what was causing the noise, I put motor oil on the OUTSIDE of about 1/3 of the belt on it stopped the squeeking!!  until it all burned off/slung off..........||||reg||8
Z||000001||GT Bastard||06-26-2000||02:33 AM||||Loosen the bolt on the bottom of the alternator and have someone else pry on the alternator with something while you re-tighten the bolt on the bottom.  That's the easiest... If you're talented, you can pry on it yourself while tightening the bolt.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||06-26-2000||02:34 AM||||oops... you'll also need to loosen the top mounting bolt on the alternator.||||reg||1
Z||000003||-=shame=-||06-26-2000||08:25 AM||||Well , if you would like a quick and easy BELT DRESSING. Had a car that needed a shot of it twice a week for two weeks and never squeaked again.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-26-2000||01:55 PM||||<B>NEVER do that again! the oiled belt is now ruined. </B> It will never be reliable no matter how much you tighten it. Worse by the time you tighten it enough to stop squeaking you'll likely have it so tight you cook off the bearings in the water pump, alternator or both.<P>When a belt squeaks, replace it. If the belt is run loose for any more than a minute or 2 it's damaged to the point it will never run properly. ((While it's off check the alternator and water pump bearings. If they feel rough as rotate the shaft or have play then the parts need to be fixed. Other wise your new belt won't last long and you are likely to soon find youself stranded.))<P>Next time you want to test for a belt slip spray it with water while it runs. That won't ruin the belt. Belt dressing also can be applied but that only tells you the belt is already shot and that you'll be replacing it soon.||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||06-26-2000||06:46 PM||||Fixed it!  Loosened the alt, took of the belt.  The belt was being rubbed by something on only half of the belt.  So I put the belt on, with the part that was being rubbed by something facing the opposite direction, put the alternater back about 1/8" from its previous spot, tightened it and so far so good.  No squeeks, no smoke from the belt or anything.......<P>I feel stupid about puting OIL on it...... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>But allwell, i'll need a new belt within the next 1000 miles anyway....||||reg||14
Z||000006||hugh||06-26-2000||09:03 PM||||I just got my Fiero and I'm not familiar with the belt setup.Where was the belt rubbing?on the front or back surface.From what you said it sounds as if there is an alignment problem.||||reg||1
Z||000007||86SE||06-27-2000||12:57 AM||||If you were to draw a line cutting the belt into 2 equal halves (just not as wide) all the dust and dirt was rubbed off of the right side.  Only half of the belt was being burned, the other side was fine, dust still covering it.  If you look closely you can see small nicks in the belt.<P>When it used to squeek, you could look through the wheel well at the crank pully and see the smoke from the belt billowing off.||||reg||1
Z||000008||hugh||06-27-2000||09:11 PM||||It sure sounds like you have a belt alignment problem.Is the rubbed part on the engine side,or the other side?If you can get a mirror and a good ,bright flashlight.Follow the belt path and look for any polished parts near the belt on the side that is wearing. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||86SE||06-27-2000||09:22 PM||||The rubbed part was the side facing away from the motor.  The water pump pulley looked like it might be a tiny bit off allignment when I turned it it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||lowCG||06-27-2000||10:15 PM||||Just don't put oil on your windshield when your wipers chatter!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||-=shame=-||06-28-2000||08:06 AM||||Oil the wipers? But gee why not? No really got another belt trauma '86 GT V-6 it has A/C but not w/o the belt. Can this be put on from underneath?||||reg||5
Z||000012||hugh||06-28-2000||07:22 PM||||Were there any polished spots that you could see?If there are no spots you can find,how do the pulleys look?Are there any rust spots on any of the pulleys(from sitting any length of time)Can you visually check the alignment?Are the parts(alternator,compressor)straight in line with the belt ,or cocked?||||reg||1
Z||000013||86SE||06-28-2000||09:53 PM||||The inner parts of all 3 pullys were polished.  The only pully that looks out of allignment is the waterpump, im pretty sure that will be going pretty soon.  At idle the waterpump makes a funny sound, anything above idle it sounds fine.  No overheating, so I know its not bad YET.||||reg||11
Z||000014||hugh||06-29-2000||08:00 PM||||If you take the belt off,can you move the waterpump pulley?there should be no movement.If it moves,replace it. ||||reg||1
